# UI quality (always on)

These rules apply to every change in this repo — library components, showcase pages, and docs chrome.

## Interactions

1. Follow the **Cursor conventions** section below. Library components must set the correct cursor themselves (not only site CSS).
2. Every interactive element needs visible **hover**, **active/press**, and **`:focus-visible`** states.
3. Prefer a short tasteful micro-interaction (120–200ms) that fits the design language (e.g. hard-shadow lift / press). Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` (no motion, keep state color changes).
4. Every nav link and button must actually be clickable on every route. Before finishing, check for overlapping layers, bad `z-index`, `pointer-events: none` on parents, and invisible overlays.

## Cursor conventions

1. `cursor: pointer` — anything that triggers an action or navigation: links, buttons, tabs, chips that are links/buttons, copy controls, checkbox/radio/toggle labels, select trigger + options, swatches, link-cards, accordion headers, close icons, command-palette rows.
2. `cursor: text` — text inputs and textareas (enabled).
3. `cursor: not-allowed` — disabled controls; never leave `pointer` on disabled.
4. `cursor: default` — non-interactive text, static cards, decorative illustrations/icons; no pointer on non-clickable chrome.
5. `cursor: progress` — loading-only buttons (still prefer `not-allowed` when also disabled).
6. `grab` / `grabbing`, `col-resize`, etc. — only for real drag/resize UI; do not fake them.

## No dead UI

5. No dead controls on showcase/demo pages. Every control either works or is removed.
6. Forms and primary actions must do something meaningful (validate, navigate, toast, animate, copy, etc.).
7. Playground controls must map to **real component props** and visibly change the preview. Never show a control that does nothing. Only expose props the component actually supports.

## Feature parity

8. When refactoring a component, list the props / variants / behaviours from the **original pre-refactor code** (git history / `main` before the refactor) and keep them unless explicitly dropped.
9. Document any intentional removals in the PR description (parity table).

## Copy & feedback

10. Copyable snippets (install commands, code blocks) need a copy affordance with visible success feedback: icon swap and/or “Copied” text, plus an `aria-live` announcement.
11. Async UI feedback (toasts, countdown, launch states) should use `aria-live` where appropriate.

## Playgrounds & color

12. Color playgrounds: provide preset swatches **and** a free color picker. The chosen value must flow into the component (prefer CSS custom properties / inline style vars).
13. Loaders/spinners must be centered, keep control width stable, and look on-brand.

## Illustrations

14. Check illustration layering/occlusion (rings that pass behind spheres, overlaps). Remove stray strokes and accidental paths.

## Accessibility

15. Basics: labels, roles, keyboard support, focus rings, contrast (WCAG AA for text), and `aria-*` for busy/disabled/expanded states.

## Metrics (no fabricated numbers)

16. Never hard-code showcase metrics that can drift (test counts, gzip sizes, star counts, component counts, “100%”, “AA”, kB badges, etc.).
17. Every displayed number must be **derived at build/runtime from the repo or an API**, with a graceful fallback that **hides** the number (never invents one). Prefer `apps/site/scripts/generate-metrics.mjs` / `metrics.generated.ts` for package stats and Vitest counts.
18. If a metric cannot be measured honestly, remove the chip/stat rather than approximating.

## Visual alignment & spacing

19. Icons inside buttons, chips, copy controls, inputs, and nav items must be **vertically and horizontally centered** (flex/grid + fixed icon box). No baseline offset, stray `line-height`, or asymmetric padding on the icon alone.
20. Use the spacing token scale (`--space-1` … `--space-12`). Prefer `gap` on stacks over ad-hoc margins. Label→field, field→field, and group→actions should share one rhythm on a given surface.
21. Sibling controls in a row (e.g. Hold/Launch) share the same height, border width, and vertical alignment. Cards in a row share content top edges; avoid unequal padding that drifts baselines.
22. Check at 1440 / 1024 / 768 / 375: no clipped focus rings, no hover that shifts layout (prefer transform/shadow), no orphaned headline words when easy to avoid, no truncated/overflowing text from fixed heights.

## Verification before finishing

23. Screenshot each touched page in **light + dark** and **desktop + mobile** when the change is visual. For alignment bugs, include zoomed crops before/after.
24. Exercise each new/changed control in the browser (or headless) before reporting done.
25. Keep CI green and ensure Vercel preview actually builds for monorepo changes (`apps/site` ignoreCommand must not skip `packages/rocket` / lockfile edits).
